{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 6500477199251234888, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 680, "mtime": 1791872299.9161563, "sha256": "7dbac838bbf54cd2e02738fedaf7fb87a358312e32efe4ddf00afd2e46702c97"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 335, "mtime": 1791872303.2160892, "sha256": "1bb07d27275be47fecdab3f0c25832571822a0590b1f20f637fae6bbdb58a2bd"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/19/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/19/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running the suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\nThere were two causes:\n1. `2.675` can't be stored exactly as a binary float. The stored value is `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round` rounds it down.\n2. Python's `round` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12` instead of `0.13`. The function's docstring promises half-up rounding.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts the number with `Decimal(repr(x))` and rounds it with `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`. `repr` gives the shortest string that converts back to the same float, so `2.675` becomes exactly `Decimal(\"2.675\")`. The function still returns a `float`, so nothing that calls it needs to change. `add_vat` uses it and gets the fix too.\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering `2.675\u21922.68`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `2.674\u21922.67`, a negative half, and an integer input. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the new test and the existing `test_split` directly with `python3`, and both passed. `add_vat(10.0)` still gives `12.0`.\n\nOne limitation remains: the fix rounds the float exactly as it prints. If arithmetic before the call produces something like `1.0049999999999999` when the intended value was `1.005`, it will round down. That can happen with the results of `add_vat`. Fully avoiding it would mean doing money calculations in `Decimal` throughout, which is a bigger change than this fix.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 250387, "requests_cache_write": 7714, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1321674, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2172, "reread": false, "rule_